#. type: Content of: <div><h1>
#: advisories.html:5
msgid "SLFS Advisories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:7
msgid ""
"This page covers advisories, notably in relation with security and changes "
"that may have broken earlier versions of the book."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:10
msgid ""
"This page is ordered like the Changelog of the book, with newest items first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: advisories.html:13
msgid "12.4 to 12.5"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: advisories.html:14
msgid "Broken changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:15
msgid ""
"Packages removed from SLFS that are in BLFS may have gotten security "
"updates. Read <a href=\"/blfs/advisories/12.4.html\">BLFS 12.4 Security "
"Advisories</a> and <a href=\"/blfs/advisories/consolidated.html\">BLFS "
"Consolidated Security Advisories</a> for such packages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:20
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-brk-12.4-003\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:21
msgid "slfs-brk-12.4-003: CUDA (Date: December 23rd, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:22
msgid ""
"The CUDA package has been moved to GLFS. NVIDIA recently released the r590 "
"major branch, dropping support for pre-Turing NVIDIA cards, and CUDA "
"followed. GLFS now has both NVIDIA r580 and r590 to support pre and post-"
"Turing. Two CUDA versions are also included for each branch.  Please refer "
"to the <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github.io/glfs/shareddeps/drivers-nvidia."
"html\">GLFS Graphics Drivers - NVIDIA</a> page for future updates to both "
"NVIDIA and CUDA's multiple versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:31
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-brk-12.4-002\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:32
msgid ""
"slfs-brk-12.4-002: nv-codec-headers (ffnvcodec) (Date: November 24th, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:33
msgid ""
"The nv-codec-headers (ffnvcodec) package has been moved to GLFS to be more "
"convenient and concise when installing the NVIDIA driver and other related "
"components. Please refer to the <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github.io/glfs/"
"shareddeps/nv-codec-headers.html\">GLFS nv-codec-headers (ffnvcodec)</a> "
"page for future updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:39
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-brk-12.4-001\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:40
msgid "slfs-brk-12.4-001: SDL3 (Date: November 18th, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:41
msgid ""
"SLFS used to provide instructions for installing SDL3 and sdl2-compat.  This "
"was done as a reference implementation of what it may look like when it'd "
"inevitably land in BLFS. Eventually, other packages like the Dolphin "
"emulator required SDL3, so it became a necessary part of SLFS. Now, BLFS has "
"SDL3 and instructions for sdl2-compat. SLFS has thus removed the "
"instructions for installing SDL3 and sdl2-compat. GLFS has followed suit "
"with BLFS. Please go to BLFS or GLFS for updates to SDL3 and sdl2-compat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: advisories.html:50
msgid "Security Advisories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:52
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-sa-12.4-004\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:53
msgid "slfs-sa-12.4-004: i3 - Rating: High (Date: December 30th, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:54
msgid ""
"In i3-4.25, along with other code improvements, the update fixed a memory "
"leak and use-after-free. These weren't assigned any IDs with any security "
"authority. To be safe, users should update to i3-4.25 or later by following "
"the <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github.io/slfs/wm/i3-wm.html\">i3 "
"installation page</a>. SysVinit and Systemd instructions for the page do not "
"differ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:62
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-sa-12.4-003\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:63
msgid "slfs-sa-12.4-003: tornado - Rating: High (Date: December 15th, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:64
msgid ""
"In tornado-6.5.3, three security vulnerabilties were fixed that could allow "
"for header injection, cross-site scription, and denial of service attacks.  "
"These security vulnerabilities have been assigned <a href=\"https://nvd.nist."
"gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67724\">CVE-2025-67724</a>, <a href=\"https://nvd."
"nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67725\">CVE-2025-67725</a>, and <a "
"href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67726\">CVE-2025-67726</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:71
msgid ""
"To update to tornado-6.5.3, follow the <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github.io/"
"slfs/general/python-dependencies.html#tornado\">tornado installation page</"
"a>. SysVinit and Systemd instructions for the page do not differ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:76
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-sa-12.4-002\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:77
msgid "slfs-sa-12.4-002: Mbed-TLS - Rating: Medium (Date: December 15th, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:78
msgid ""
"In Mbed-TLS-3.6.5, two security vulnerabilties were fixed that could allow "
"for partial recovery of CBC-PKCS7-encrypted plaintext and private key "
"material disclosure.  These security vulnerabilities have been assigned <a "
"href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-54764\">CVE-2025-54764</a> "
"and <a href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/"
"CVE-2025-59438\">CVE-2025-59438</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:84
msgid ""
"To update to Mbed-TLS-3.6.5, follow the <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github."
"io/slfs/general/mbedtls.html\">Mbed-TLS installation page</a>. SysVinit and "
"Systemd instructions for the page do not differ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div>
#: advisories.html:89
msgid "<a id=\"slfs-sa-12.4-001\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h4>
#: advisories.html:90
msgid "slfs-sa-12.4-001: OpenJDK-17 - Rating: High (Date: October 23rd, 2025)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:91
msgid ""
"In OpenJDK-17.0.17-ga, two security vulnerabilties were fixed that could "
"allow for exploitation of APIs via multiple network protocols, leading to "
"creation, modification, and deletion of data. This is especially an issue "
"with Minecraft servers, as an affected JDK version will have elevated "
"privileges because of calls to mods/modpacks. These vulnerabilities affect "
"other major JDK versions. If you have multiple OpenJDK versions built, "
"update all of them if there is an update present.  These security "
"vulnerabilities have been assigned <a href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/"
"detail/CVE-2025-53057\">CVE-2025-53057</a> and <a href=\"https://nvd.nist."
"gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-53066\">CVE-2025-53066</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: advisories.html:101
msgid ""
"To update to OpenJDK-17.0.17-ga, follow the <a href=\"https://glfs-book."
"github.io/slfs/general/openjdk.html\">OpenJDK installation page</a>. "
"SysVinit and Systemd instructions for the page do not differ. The Java page "
"also has the new version."
msgstr ""
